sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Staff (Admin or Employee)
    actor K as Kunde
    participant AO as Admin/Orders
    participant PC as Profile or Confirmation
    participant OS as SqlOrderStore
    participant DB as MarsvinDb
    participant AL as IAuditLogStore
    participant OE as OrderEmails

    Note over S,OE: What happens to an order after checkout.

    S->>AO: POST status (orderId, new status, tracking number)
    Note over AO: [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Employee")]<br/>The tracking number may only hold letters, digits, spaces and dashes,<br/>and is dropped for a pickup order whatever the form says.
    AO->>OS: FindById(orderId)

    alt new status is Cancelled
        AO->>OS: Cancel(orderId, latest = Processing)
        Note over AO,OS: Staff may cancel until the order has been sent.
    else any other status
        AO->>OS: UpdateStatus(orderId, status, trackingNumber)
        OS->>DB: UPDATE Orders SET Status, TrackingNumber<br/>WHERE OrderId = @id AND Status <> Cancelled
        Note over OS,DB: A cancelled order is final - its items<br/>are already back on sale.
    end

    alt nothing changed (already sent, or already cancelled)
        AO-->>S: error message
    else changed
        AO->>AL: Record("Order.StatusChanged", "#id: old -> new")
        AO->>OE: SendStatusUpdateAsync(order)
        Note over AO,OE: Staff triggered it, so the mail is written in<br/>Orders.PlacedInEnglish - the language the buyer ordered in,<br/>not the language of the staff member's browser.
        OE-->>K: email: being prepared / sent, with tracking number /<br/>ready for pickup / delivered / cancelled
        AO-->>S: "order updated, the customer has been emailed"
    end

    K->>PC: POST cancel (orderId)
    Note over PC: From the receipt or the order history.<br/>First the order is looked up the same way as for viewing it:<br/>it has to be the caller's own.
    PC->>OS: Cancel(orderId, latest = Placed)
    Note over PC,OS: The buyer may cancel only until staff<br/>have started preparing the order.
    OS->>DB: BeginTransaction
    OS->>DB: UPDATE Orders SET Status = Cancelled<br/>WHERE OrderId = @id AND Status <= @latest
    Note over OS,DB: One statement both checks and changes - a second click,<br/>or two requests at once, find nothing left to cancel.
    alt no row changed
        OS->>DB: Rollback
        OS-->>PC: false
        PC-->>K: "can no longer be cancelled"
    else cancelled
        loop each order line
            OS->>DB: accessory: StockQuantity = StockQuantity + qty<br/>animal: Status Sold -> Available
        end
        OS->>DB: Commit
        OS-->>PC: true
        PC->>OE: SendStatusUpdateAsync(order, language of the buyer's own browser)
        OE-->>K: email: order cancelled
        PC-->>K: order shown as Cancelled
    end

    Note over S,OE: Cancelled is the highest status number, so "may still be cancelled"<br/>is a plain Status <= latest comparison that a cancelled order can never pass.
